: "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Superlative Adjectives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use a superlative to compare somebody or something to the whole group that he, she or it belongs to. <br><br> Look at the chart for information on how to form the superlative:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjective\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Superlative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tall <bR> old\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tallest <br>oldest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Most adjectives:  <br>+ -est\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"late<br> nice\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"latest <br>nicest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjectives ending in -e:  <br>+-st\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"happy<br> lucky\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"happiest <br>luckiest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"2-syllable adjectives ending in -y: <br> +iest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"attractive <br>intelligent <br>beautiful\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"most attractive <br>most intelligent <br>most beautiful\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"3+-syllable adjectives:  <br>most + adjective\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"good <br> bad\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the best <br>the worst\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Irregular comparisons\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You add <span class=\"strong\">the</span> in front of the superlative form to describe people, places and things."}, {"type": "example", "content": "He is <span class=\"underline\">the most attractive</span> man in the city."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I am <span class=\"underline\">the luckiest</span> woman."}, {"type": "example", "content": "He is <span class=\"underline\">the cutest</span> boy in the world."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Reacting to a Story"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When someone tells you a story, it is important to react to show that you are listening and that you are interested."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When someone tells you a story, it is important to react to show that you are listening and that you are interested."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Oh, really? <br>Wow! <br>That's interesting! <br>Tell me more! <br>I can't believe that! <br>What do you mean?"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "strange "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "odd; unusual"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Everyone I meet is really strange!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le06ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to describe someone."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wild"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "crazy; not normal"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She was acting wild."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le06ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rude"}, {"type": "definition", 